body:
I have the same issue as reported in https://github.com/jgromes/RadioLib/issues/1434 where an XTAL LR1121 radio module (the GNiceRF Lora1121) that is initialised as a TCXO module hangs on startup. The answer at the time was to specify the correct radio (of course). However, I make a lot of DIY radio sets using the NRF Promicro and its useful to have the "TCXO_Optional" feature that Meshtastic provides where it tries in both TCXO and XTAL modes.

Looking at the code (with LLM assistance) it looks like the issue identified at the time was that the calibration never completes and it enters a permanent busy loop which doesn't time out. This is not the case with the GNiceRF Lora2021, incidentally, which is also an XTAL module.

I have a workaround where XTAL is probed first, then TCXO, but it would be good if the loop could be closed so the same outcome is achieved as for the SX1262 and LR2021.

I took the liberty of asking Clod to come up with a solution, and it gave this:


## Proposed fix

Bound both loops with the same 3-second timeout pattern already used for the erase-wait,
returning `RADIOLIB_ERR_SPI_CMD_TIMEOUT` (an error code downstream TCXO-optional fallbacks
already treat as "retry without TCXO", same as `RADIOLIB_ERR_SPI_CMD_FAILED`):

```diff
--- a/src/modules/LR11x0/LR11x0.cpp
+++ b/src/modules/LR11x0/LR11x0.cpp
@@ int16_t LR11x0::config(uint8_t modem) {
   // calibrate all blocks
   state = this->calibrate(RADIOLIB_LR11X0_CALIBRATE_ALL);

-  // wait for calibration completion
+  // wait for calibration completion (bounded - if the configured TCXO reference never
+  // locks, e.g. no TCXO physically present, BUSY/GPIO can otherwise stay asserted forever).
+  // Skip the wait entirely if the calibrate command itself already failed/timed out.
   this->mod->hal->delay(5);
-  while(this->mod->hal->digitalRead(this->mod->getGpio())) {
+  RadioLibTime_t calStart = this->mod->hal->millis();
+  while((state == RADIOLIB_ERR_NONE) && this->mod->hal->digitalRead(this->mod->getGpio())) {
+    if(this->mod->hal->millis() - calStart >= 3000) {
+      RADIOLIB_DEBUG_BASIC_PRINTLN("BUSY pin timeout after calibration!");
+      return(RADIOLIB_ERR_SPI_CMD_TIMEOUT);
+    }
     this->mod->hal->yield();
   }
```

I can attach my instrumented boot logs if it would help further, although I think there's enough to get an idea of what might be needed.

Many thanks!
